<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>glockpeek · set up encryption</title>
  <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/logo.png" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Courier+Prime:wght@400;700&family=Crimson+Pro:wght@400;600;700&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    /* Harmonised with the dashboard: warm paper, fountain-pen ink, one red accent,
       Crimson Pro headings + Inter body + Courier Prime for keys/code. */
    :root {
      --bg:#f1ebdd; --panel:#fbfaf6; --well:#f6f1e7; --line:#e4ddcc; --ink:#22324e;
      --dim:#556480; --accent:#c0564a; --ok:#5f8169;
      --sans:"Inter",system-ui,sans-serif; --display:"Crimson Pro",Georgia,serif; --mono:"Courier Prime",ui-monospace,monospace;
    }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body { margin:0; background:var(--bg); color:var(--ink); font-family:var(--sans); line-height:1.5; }
    .wrap { max-width: 560px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 48px 20px 80px; }
    h1 { font-family:var(--display); font-size: 2rem; margin: 0 0 2px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing:-.01em; text-transform:lowercase; }
    h1 span { color: var(--accent); }
    .tag { color: var(--dim); font-size: .95rem; margin: 0 0 32px; }
    .card { background:var(--panel); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:6px; padding:24px; margin-bottom:20px; box-shadow:2px 3px 0 rgba(34,50,78,.05); }
    h2 { font-family:var(--display); font-size:1.3rem; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 12px; }
    p { color:var(--dim); font-size:.95rem; }
    label { display:block; font-size:.9rem; margin:16px 0 6px; color:var(--ink); }
    input[type=password] { width:100%; padding:10px 12px; background:var(--well); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:6px; color:var(--ink); font-size:1rem; font-family:var(--mono); }
    input:focus { outline:none; border-color:var(--accent); box-shadow:0 0 0 2px rgba(192,86,74,.15); }
    button { font:inherit; font-weight:600; cursor:pointer; border:none; border-radius:6px; padding:11px 18px; }
    .primary { background:var(--accent); color:#fbfaf6; width:100%; margin-top:20px; }
    .primary:disabled { opacity:.5; cursor:not-allowed; }
    .ghost { background:transparent; color:var(--dim); border:1px solid var(--line); }
    .ghost:hover { color:var(--ink); }
    a { color:var(--accent); }
    .err { color:var(--accent); font-size:.9rem; min-height:1.2em; margin-top:10px; }
    .hint { font-size:.85rem; color:var(--dim); margin-top:6px; }
    .hint code, p code { font-family:var(--mono); background:var(--well); padding:1px 5px; border-radius:3px; font-size:.9em; }
    .code { font-family:var(--mono); font-size:1.15rem; letter-spacing:.06em; word-break:break-all; background:var(--well); border:1px dashed var(--accent); border-radius:6px; padding:16px; margin:14px 0; color:var(--ink); }
    .warn { border-left:3px solid var(--accent); padding-left:12px; }
    .ok { color:var(--ok); }
    .hidden { display:none; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>glock<span>peek</span></h1>
    <p class="tag">end-to-end encryption setup</p>

    <div id="loading" class="card"><p>Checking your account…</p></div>

    <!-- Not signed in -->
    <div id="need-login" class="card hidden">
      <h2>Sign in first</h2>
      <p>You need to be signed in to set up encryption. <a href="/">Go to the dashboard</a> and sign in, then come back here.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Already configured -->
    <div id="already" class="card hidden">
      <h2 class="ok">Encryption is already set up</h2>
      <p>This account already has an encryption vault. Your synced records are protected by a master key that only your passphrase (or recovery code) can unlock.</p>
      <p class="warn">Setting up again would create a <strong>new</strong> master key and make any data encrypted under the old key unreadable. Only do that if you've lost both your passphrase and recovery code.</p>
      <button id="reset-btn" class="ghost">Set up a new key anyway…</button>
    </div>

    <!-- Passphrase form -->
    <div id="form-card" class="card hidden">
      <h2>Choose a passphrase</h2>
      <p>Your records are encrypted on your machine before they're synced here. The server stores only encrypted data — it never sees your passphrase or your key. If you lose <em>both</em> your passphrase and your recovery code, your history can't be recovered.</p>
      <form id="form">
        <label for="pass">Passphrase</label>
        <input id="pass" type="password" autocomplete="new-password" minlength="12" placeholder="at least 12 characters" />
        <div class="hint">Four random words make a strong passphrase. e.g. <code>copper-mango-drift-lantern</code> or <code>quiet river seven maple</code> (pick your own).</div>
        <label for="pass2">Confirm passphrase</label>
        <input id="pass2" type="password" autocomplete="new-password" placeholder="type it again" />
        <div class="err" id="form-err"></div>
        <button type="submit" class="primary" id="submit">Create encryption key</button>
      </form>
    </div>

    <!-- Recovery code -->
    <div id="done-card" class="card hidden">
      <h2 class="ok">Encryption is on</h2>
      <p class="warn">Save this recovery code somewhere safe (a password manager, on paper). It's the <strong>only</strong> way back in if you forget your passphrase. We can't recover it for you — it never leaves your browser.</p>
      <div class="code" id="recovery-code"></div>
      <button id="copy-btn" class="ghost">Copy code</button>
      <label style="margin-top:22px;"><input type="checkbox" id="saved-check" /> I've saved my recovery code</label>
      <button id="finish-btn" class="primary" disabled>Go to dashboard</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script type="module" src="/encryption-setup.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
